<http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p0323gx5nk4> a skos:Concept ;
    periodo:spatialCoverageDescription "Earth" ;
    dcelements:language "en" ;
    dcterms:language <http://lexvo.org/id/iso639-1/en> ;
    dcterms:spatial <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q2> ;
    skos:altLabel "Energy epoch one: geochemical energy"@en ;
    skos:editorialNote "The source notes that these epochs are agglomerative: that is, the geochemical epoch does not stop when the sunlight epoch begins, but continues to the present. For the sake of clarity, however, I have marked an end where a given form of energy generation ceases to be the predominant one." ;
    skos:inScheme <http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p0323gx> ;
    skos:note "\"For [the start of this epoch] I have taken the earliest date for which there is evidence consistent with life\", citing Bell, E. A., Boehnke, P., Harrison, T. M. & Mao, W. L. Potentially biogenic carbon preserved in a 4.1 billion-year-old zircon. Proc. Natl Acad. Sci. USA 112, 14518–14521 (2015)." ;
    skos:prefLabel "Energy epoch one: geochemical energy" ;
    time:intervalFinishedBy [ skos:prefLabel "3.7 Ga" ;
            time:hasDateTimeDescription [ time:year "-3700000000"^^xsd:gYear ] ] ;
    time:intervalStartedBy [ skos:prefLabel "4.1 Ga" ;
            time:hasDateTimeDescription [ time:year "-4560000000"^^xsd:gYear ] ] .

<http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p0323gxcztt> a skos:Concept ;
    periodo:spatialCoverageDescription "Earth" ;
    dcelements:language "en" ;
    dcterms:language <http://lexvo.org/id/iso639-1/en> ;
    dcterms:spatial <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q2> ;
    skos:altLabel "Energy epoch two: sunlight"@en ;
    skos:editorialNote "The source notes that these epochs are agglomerative: that is, the geochemical epoch does not stop when the sunlight epoch begins, but continues to the present. For the sake of clarity, however, I have marked an end where a given form of energy generation ceases to be the predominant one. The end of this epoch is given as the range of the Great Oxidation Event." ;
    skos:inScheme <http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p0323gx> ;
    skos:note "\"For [the start of this epoch] I have taken the earliest date for which there is evidence consistent with photosynthesis\", citing Rosing, M. 13C-depleted carbon microparticles in >3700-Ma sea-floor sedimentary rocks from west Greenland. Science 283, 674–676 (1999); Pecoits, E. et al. Atmospheric hydrogen peroxide and Eoarchean iron formations. Geobiology 13, 1–14 (2015); Nutman, A. P., Bennett, V. C., Friend, C. R. L., Van Kranendonk, M. J. & Chivas, A. R. Rapid emergence of life shown by discovery of 3,700-million-year-old microbial structures. Nature 537, 535–538 (2016)." ;
    skos:prefLabel "Energy epoch two: sunlight" ;
    time:intervalFinishedBy [ skos:prefLabel "2.45 Ga to 2.32 Ga" ;
            time:hasDateTimeDescription [ periodo:earliestYear "-2450000000"^^xsd:gYear ;
                    periodo:latestYear "-2320000000"^^xsd:gYear ] ] ;
    time:intervalStartedBy [ skos:prefLabel "3.7 Ga" ;
            time:hasDateTimeDescription [ time:year "-3700000000"^^xsd:gYear ] ] .

<http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p0323gxds6f> a skos:Concept ;
    periodo:spatialCoverageDescription "Earth" ;
    dcelements:language "en" ;
    dcterms:language <http://lexvo.org/id/iso639-1/en> ;
    dcterms:spatial <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q2> ;
    skos:altLabel "Energy epoch five: fire"@en ;
    skos:editorialNote "The current epoch has no real end date, since this source of energy has not yet been superceded by another." ;
    skos:inScheme <http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p0323gx> ;
    skos:note "Source identifies two phases, the earliest of which begins with \"the evolution of a fire creature... [that] began to control the use of fire, deliberately setting fires alight and using fire for cooking,\" and the later of which might be given a beginning at a number of key points (\"the burning of fossil fuels such as coal to generate heat and light\", \"the invention of the internal combustion engine\", or \"the discovery of the Haber-Bosch process for fixing nitrogen\")." ;
    skos:prefLabel "Energy epoch five: fire" ;
    time:intervalFinishedBy [ skos:prefLabel "today" ;
            time:hasDateTimeDescription [ time:year "2017"^^xsd:gYear ] ] ;
    time:intervalStartedBy [ skos:prefLabel "From 1.5 Ma to 0.4 Ma" ;
            time:hasDateTimeDescription [ periodo:earliestYear "-1500000"^^xsd:gYear ;
                    periodo:latestYear "-40000"^^xsd:gYear ] ] .

<http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p0323gxrm53> a skos:Concept ;
    periodo:spatialCoverageDescription "Earth" ;
    dcelements:language "en" ;
    dcterms:language <http://lexvo.org/id/iso639-1/en> ;
    dcterms:spatial <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q2> ;
    skos:altLabel "Energy epoch three: oxygen"@en ;
    skos:editorialNote "The source notes that these epochs are agglomerative: that is, the geochemical epoch does not stop when the sunlight epoch begins, but continues to the present. For the sake of clarity, however, I have marked an end where a given form of energy generation ceases to be the predominant one. " ;
    skos:inScheme <http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p0323gx> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Energy epoch three: oxygen" ;
    time:intervalFinishedBy [ skos:prefLabel "575 Ma" ;
            time:hasDateTimeDescription [ time:year "-575000000"^^xsd:gYear ] ] ;
    time:intervalStartedBy [ skos:prefLabel "Between 2.45 and 2.32 Ga (The Great Oxidation Event)" ;
            time:hasDateTimeDescription [ periodo:earliestYear "-2450000000"^^xsd:gYear ;
                    periodo:latestYear "-2320000000"^^xsd:gYear ] ] .

<http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p0323gxv8wc> a skos:Concept ;
    periodo:spatialCoverageDescription "Earth" ;
    dcelements:language "en" ;
    dcterms:language <http://lexvo.org/id/iso639-1/en> ;
    dcterms:spatial <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q2> ;
    skos:altLabel "Energy epoch four: flesh"@en ;
