    skos:note "From \"A description of a new chart of History\", 6th ed., 1786, p. 85: \"... the first foreign invasion of China was made by the Kitans in 946. In 949 some cities in the northern parts were relinquished to them, and in 950 they made further conquests. In 1117 the Kin Tartars, at the invitation of princes of the Song dynasty, who reigned in the southern parts of China, invaded and destroyed the empire of the Kitans, but at the same time made the Song themselves tributary.\"" ;
