<http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p05hrsfbf96> a skos:Concept ;
    periodo:spatialCoverageDescription "Thibet" ;
    dcelements:language "en" ;
    dcterms:language <http://lexvo.org/id/iso639-1/en> ;
    dcterms:source [ dcterms:isPartOf <http://www.worldcat.org/oclc/82293509> ;
            bibo:locator "Row labeled \"China\"" ] ;
    dcterms:spatial <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q17252> ;
    skos:altLabel "Thibet"@en ;
    skos:editorialNote """The chart depicts years with a chronological line at the top, radiating from a center point of the birth of Christ. "BC" has been added to the entries where required as illustrated by the structure of the chart, but not actually written.
Spatial coverage has been determined by the labels on the chart running along the right side, separated across the chart with horizontal lines, and narrowed within each horizontal line by smaller areas. In the case of the spatial coverage of the value "Thibet", which for Priestley does not seem to match modern national boundaries, we have used the countries where the geopolitical phenomena he associates with "Thibet" (e.g. the Tangut Empire) took place.

The start date for this period is marked as uncertain in the text and the chart, but is aligned with the date assigned to the Mongol subjection to the Qing Dynasty in 1582.

""" ;
    skos:inScheme <http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p05hrsf> ;
    skos:note "From \"A description of a new chart of History\", 6th ed., 1786, p. 84: \"At what time this country became independent of the Tartars is not known, but in 1716 Thibet, the remains of it, was conquered by the Chinese.\"" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Thibet" ;
    time:intervalFinishedBy [ skos:prefLabel "1716" ;
            time:hasDateTimeDescription [ time:year "1716"^^xsd:gYear ] ] ;
    time:intervalStartedBy [ skos:prefLabel "around 1582" ;
            time:hasDateTimeDescription [ time:year "1582"^^xsd:gYear ] ] .

<http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p05hrsfbqw9> a skos:Concept ;
    periodo:spatialCoverageDescription "Leautong" ;
    dcelements:language "en" ;
    dcterms:language <http://lexvo.org/id/iso639-1/en> ;
    dcterms:source [ dcterms:isPartOf <http://www.worldcat.org/oclc/82293509> ;
            bibo:locator "Row labeled \"China\"" ] ;
    dcterms:spatial <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q148>,
        <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q483134> ;
    skos:altLabel "Empire of Leoutong"@en ;
    skos:editorialNote """The chart depicts years with a chronological line at the top, radiating from a center point of the birth of Christ. "BC" has been added to the entries where required as illustrated by the structure of the chart, but not actually written.
Spatial coverage has been determined by the labels on the chart running along the right side, separated across the chart with horizontal lines, and narrowed within each horizontal line by smaller areas.
Ending dates of 1770 derived from the year of publication, and also the point at which the chart ends.

Leautong was a region northwest of the Korean peninsula, between Korea and China.""" ;
    skos:inScheme <http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p05hrsf> ;
    skos:note "From \"A description of a new chart of History\", 6th ed., 1786, s.v. Leautong, p. 86: \"This empire began about 811, and the inhabitants of this country, called Kitans, being increased by many colonies from Korea in 1033, became very considerable, and changed their name to Lyau. In 1011 this empire was destroyed by the Chinese, in conjunction with the Niuche, or Eastern Tartars, who immediately established themselves in this country, which is in the northern parts of China.\"" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Empire of Leautong" ;
    time:intervalFinishedBy [ skos:prefLabel "1101" ;
            time:hasDateTimeDescription [ time:year "1101"^^xsd:gYear ] ] ;
    time:intervalStartedBy [ skos:prefLabel "about 811" ;
            time:hasDateTimeDescription [ time:year "0811"^^xsd:gYear ] ] .

<http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p05hrsfbrjk> a skos:Concept ;
    periodo:spatialCoverageDescription "Egypt" ;
    dcelements:language "en" ;
    dcterms:language <http://lexvo.org/id/iso639-1/en> ;
    dcterms:source [ bibo:locator "Row labeled \"Africa\"" ] ;
    dcterms:spatial <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q79> ;
    skos:altLabel "Egyptians"@en ;
    skos:editorialNote "Although this range overlaps with the \"Shepherd Kings\" and includes a period in which Egypt seems to control the \"Ethiopians\" between 1010 and 955 BC, Priestley's references are not clear enough to parse into multiple periods in different places, so the \"Egyptian\" segment here encompasses the entire chronological range but excludes Sudan and Ethiopia. Priestley is probably differentiating between Lower Egypt and the Delta (where he places the Shepherd Kings), Upper Egypt (always ruled by Egyptians), and the northern parts of Nubia, where Egypt made incursions at the end of the New Kingdom." ;
    skos:inScheme <http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p05hrsf> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Egyptians" ;
    time:intervalFinishedBy [ skos:prefLabel "945 BC" ;
            time:hasDateTimeDescription [ time:year "-0944"^^xsd:gYear ] ] ;
    time:intervalStartedBy [ skos:prefLabel "1200 BC" ;
            time:hasDateTimeDescription [ time:year "-1199"^^xsd:gYear ] ] .

