    skos:editorialNote "Priestley distinguishes between the absolute rule of the Japanese Emperor and the period of the Shoguns. Although the Shogunate technically began in 1192, Priestley seems to begin this period with Minamoto no Yoritomo's (\"Jerotimo\") rise to power from 1185." ;
    skos:inScheme <http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p05hrsf> ;
    skos:note "From \"A description of a new chart of History\", 6th ed., 1786, s.v. \"Japan\", pp. 86-87: \"Sin-onu, an ecclesiastic, is said to have founded the Japanese monarchy, about 660 B.C. but in 1188 Jerotimo put an end to the supreme ecclesiastic authority, and became the first secular monarch of Japan.\"" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Secular monarchs of Japan" ;
    time:intervalFinishedBy [ skos:prefLabel "1770" ;
