<http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p05hrsfqfjp> a skos:Concept ;
    periodo:spatialCoverageDescription "Indostan" ;
    dcelements:language "en" ;
    dcterms:language <http://lexvo.org/id/iso639-1/en> ;
    dcterms:source [ dcterms:isPartOf <http://www.worldcat.org/oclc/82293509> ;
            bibo:locator "Row labeled \"India\"" ] ;
    dcterms:spatial <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q43100>,
        <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q668>,
        <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q843>,
        <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q889> ;
    skos:altLabel "Moghul Empire"@en,
        "Mogul Empire"@en,
        "Mughal Empire"@en,
        "TarTars in Indostan"@en,
        "Timurid Empire"@en ;
    skos:editorialNote """The chart depicts years with a chronological line at the top, radiating from a center point of the birth of Christ. "BC" has been added to the entries where required as illustrated by the structure of the chart, but not actually written.
Spatial coverage has been determined by the labels on the chart running along the right side, separated across the chart with horizontal lines, and narrowed within each horizontal line by smaller areas.
Ending dates of 1770 derived from the year of publication, and also the point at which the chart ends.

With the exception of the area occupied by the former Ghaznavid dynasty, where the 14th-century succession was Timurid, the "Tartars" in Indostan seem to be the Mughal dynasty from 1530 onward.""" ;
    skos:inScheme <http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p05hrsf> ;
    skos:note "From \"A description of a new chart of History\", 6th ed., 1786, s.v. Indostan, pp. 82-83: \"...in 1383 Timur Bek conquered Candahar. In 1396 he invaded the rest of India, and in 1399 he entered Delhi the capital of it, conquering the remains of Mahmud Gazni's empire\"; p. 83: \"when Sultan Babr was expelled from Buccharia by the Usbeks, he was obliged to fight his way into India, where he firmly established himself in 1530, and conquered the whole of it, except Decan, Guzerat, and Bengal. In 1538 Bengal was conquered by the Great Moguls (as the reigning princes of this family were then called) and about 1558 Guzerat was conquered by Akbar, who also conquered Candahar, which had become independent. In 1621 Shah Abbas of Persia conquered Candahar. In 1687 Golkonda and Visapour were conquered by the Moguls.\"" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Tartars in Indostan" ;
