<http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p05hrsftkgs> a skos:Concept ;
    periodo:spatialCoverageDescription "China; Leautong" ;
    dcelements:language "en" ;
    dcterms:language <http://lexvo.org/id/iso639-1/en> ;
    dcterms:source [ dcterms:isPartOf <http://www.worldcat.org/oclc/82293509> ;
            bibo:locator "Row labeled \"China\"" ] ;
    dcterms:spatial <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q148> ;
    skos:altLabel "Kin"@en ;
    skos:editorialNote """The chart depicts years with a chronological line at the top, radiating from a center point of the birth of Christ. "BC" has been added to the entries where required as illustrated by the structure of the chart, but not actually written.
Spatial coverage has been determined by the labels on the chart running along the right side, separated across the chart with horizontal lines, and narrowed within each horizontal line by smaller areas.
Ending dates of 1770 derived from the year of publication, and also the point at which the chart ends.

In "A description of a new chart of History", the spatial reference here is to China, although the space on the timeline occupies the same row as the "Empire of Leautong" and the Kitans. "Leautong" is treated as a separate northern state in China.""" ;
    skos:inScheme <http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p05hrsf> ;
    skos:note "From \"A description of a new chart of History\", 6th ed., 1786, p. 85: \"In 1117 the Kin Tartars, at the invitation of the princes of the Song dynasty, who reigned in the southern parts of China, invaded and destroyed the empire of the Kitans, but at the same time made the Song themselves tributary. In 1211 Jenghis Khan invaded China, and in 1234 his son Oktay put an end to the dynasty of the Kin.\"" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Kin" ;
    time:intervalFinishedBy [ skos:prefLabel "1234" ;
            time:hasDateTimeDescription [ time:year "1234"^^xsd:gYear ] ] ;
    time:intervalStartedBy [ skos:prefLabel "1117" ;
            time:hasDateTimeDescription [ time:year "1117"^^xsd:gYear ] ] .

