    skos:editorialNote "This LCSH record seems to have been reconciled by the Ngā Upoko Tukutuku / Māori Subject Headings service of the New Zealand National Library as Ngā Pakanga Whenua o Mua (https://natlib.govt.nz/nga-upoko-tukutuku/ng%C4%81-pakanga-whenua-o-mua), preferred to Ngā Pakanga o Aotearoa (https://natlib.govt.nz/nga-upoko-tukutuku/ng%C4%81-pakanga-o-aotearoa)." ;
    skos:inScheme <http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p06c6g3> ;
    skos:note "Extracted from heading \"New Zealand--History--New Zealand Wars, 1843-1847\". Added to LCSH in 2004. Sources cited: Belich, J. The New Zealand wars and the Victorian interpretation of racial conflict, 1986: p. 204 (three local outbreaks of conflict took place between 1843 and 1847) p. 212 (The period 1847-60 was one of peace between Māori and Pākehā); Oxford hist. of N.Z., 1981: p. 148 (The central role of land in the wars between Māori and Pāehā has often been remarked; sometimes they have been called the Land Wars); The New Zealand Wars web site, Sept. 19, 2003 (The New Zealand Wars were fought in New Zealand between 1843 and 1872) what's in a name (the Maori Wars; the Land Wars; Nga Pakanga Nu Nui o Aotearoa; Nga pakanga o Aotearoa; the Anglo-Maori Wars; the Colonial New Zealand Wars; new Zealand Civil Wars; the overwhelmingly favourite name used these days is undoubtedly the New Zealand Wars)." ;
