    skos:altLabel "Mahdiya"@en ;
    skos:inScheme <http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p08m57h> ;
    skos:note "The term refers to the period between 1881 and 1898 of the Sudanese nationalist movement led by Mohamed Ahmed al-Mahdi (the Mahdi) against the Turkiya which led to the capture of  Khartoum in 1885. After his death in 1885, Mohamed Ahmed is succeeded by Abdullahi ibn Mohamed (the Khalifa) who ruled until his defeat at the battle of Omdurman by General Kitchener in 1898." ;
    skos:prefLabel "Mahdiya" ;
    time:intervalFinishedBy [ skos:prefLabel "1898" ;
