<http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p08m57h35dv> a skos:Concept ;
    periodo:spatialCoverageDescription "Zagros region" ;
    dcelements:language "en" ;
    dcterms:language <http://lexvo.org/id/iso639-1/en> ;
    dcterms:spatial <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q43>,
        <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q794>,
        <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q796> ;
    owl:sameAs <http://collection.britishmuseum.org/id/thesauri/x113394> ;
    skos:altLabel "Kakwayhid dynasty"@en ;
    skos:inScheme <http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p08m57h> ;
    skos:note "1008-1051 (AH 398-AH 443). Petty Kurdish and Daylami dynasty of the Zagros region when the power of the Buyids (q.v.) began to fade. With the rise of the Seljuqs in Persia the Kakwayhid's lost their independence and were reduced to vasaledge. Muhammad known as Ibn Kakuya, who was the son of Dushmanziyar, was the governor of Isfahan in 1008 (AH 398). He soon expanded his power to Hamadan and Kurdistan and his court circle included the philosopher and physian Ibn Sina (Avicenna) who functioned as his vizier." ;
    skos:prefLabel "Kakwayhid dynasty" ;
    time:intervalFinishedBy [ skos:prefLabel "1051 (AH 443)" ;
            time:hasDateTimeDescription [ time:year "1051"^^xsd:gYear ] ] ;
    time:intervalStartedBy [ skos:prefLabel "1008 (AH 398)" ;
            time:hasDateTimeDescription [ time:year "1008"^^xsd:gYear ] ] ;
    foaf:page <http://collection.britishmuseum.org/id/thesauri/x113394> .

