<http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p08m57h6mcm> a skos:Concept ;
    periodo:spatialCoverageDescription "Daylam" ;
    dcelements:language "en" ;
    dcterms:language <http://lexvo.org/id/iso639-1/en> ;
    dcterms:spatial <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q794> ;
    owl:sameAs <http://collection.britishmuseum.org/id/thesauri/x52034> ;
    skos:altLabel "Ziyarid dynasty"@en ;
    skos:inScheme <http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p08m57h> ;
    skos:note "931-c.1090 (AH 319-AH 413). Local dynasty in the remote highland region of Daylam at the south-west corner of the Caspian Sea. The Ziyarids descended from Mardawij ibn Ziyar of the royal clan of Gilan. His power extended as far south as Isfahan and Hamadan but he was murdered in 935 (AH 323) by his own Turkish slave troops. The Ziyarids lost their power but Mardawij's brother, Wushmgir, retained a foot hold in the eastern Caspian provinces by acknowledging as his overlords the Samanids. In the 11th century the Ziyarids has to recognise the overlordship of the Ghnazvids and survived as vassals of the Seljuqs in the highland region." ;
    skos:prefLabel "Ziyarid dynasty" ;
    time:intervalFinishedBy [ skos:prefLabel "c. 1090 (AH 413)" ;
            time:hasDateTimeDescription [ time:year "1090"^^xsd:gYear ] ] ;
    time:intervalStartedBy [ skos:prefLabel "931 (AH 319)" ;
            time:hasDateTimeDescription [ time:year "0931"^^xsd:gYear ] ] ;
    foaf:page <http://collection.britishmuseum.org/id/thesauri/x52034> .

