<http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p08m57h6tvb> a skos:Concept ;
    periodo:spatialCoverageDescription "Cyprus" ;
    dcelements:language "en" ;
    dcterms:language <http://lexvo.org/id/iso639-1/en> ;
    dcterms:spatial <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q229> ;
    owl:sameAs <http://collection.britishmuseum.org/id/thesauri/x105793> ;
    skos:altLabel "Middle Cypriot"@en ;
    skos:inScheme <http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p08m57h> ;
    skos:note "ca. 1900 BC-1650 BC. The second division of the Cypriot Bronze Age, marking an expansion in the range of pottery types (including White Painted wares which appeared at the end of the EC period), the spread of settlements all over the island (including fortified sites) and the first signs of significant overseas contacts in the form of numerous ceramic exports to surrounding regions. Many artefacts types, including metal goods, are similar to those from the EC and continue in use into the LC. The last phase of Middle Cypriot, MCIII, witnesses a major increase in the economic and cultural dynamism of the island, including the establishment of new coastal settlements." ;
    skos:prefLabel "Middle Cypriot" ;
    time:intervalFinishedBy [ skos:prefLabel "1650 BC" ;
            time:hasDateTimeDescription [ time:year "-1649"^^xsd:gYear ] ] ;
    time:intervalStartedBy [ skos:prefLabel "ca. 1900 BC" ;
            time:hasDateTimeDescription [ time:year "-1899"^^xsd:gYear ] ] ;
    foaf:page <http://collection.britishmuseum.org/id/thesauri/x105793> .

