    skos:note "The Karts or Kurts of eastern Khurasan and northern Afghanistan were an indiginous dynasty who claimed to be heirs of the Ghurids. The Mongols allowed Shams al-Din I Muhammad (1245-1277, AH 643-676) to rule as a vassal prince in Herat and the mountains of Ghur. They remained loyal allies of the Il-Khans of Persia." ;
