    skos:altLabel "Samanid dynasty"@en ;
    skos:inScheme <http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p08m57h> ;
    skos:note "819-1005 (AH 204-AH 395). Dynasty of local land owners in Khurasan and Transoxania who claimed descent from pre-Islamic Sasanian emperors of Iran. New Persian language and literature flourished under Samanid rule. In the middle of the 10th century a series of revolts resulted in decentralisation and enabled the Qarakhanids and Ghaznavids to cease control over Samanid territories in 1005 (AH 395)." ;
    skos:prefLabel "Samanid dynasty" ;
    time:intervalFinishedBy [ skos:prefLabel "1005 (AH 395)" ;
