    skos:inScheme <http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p08m57h> ;
    skos:note "The Old Hittite kingdom begins in the late sixteenth century BC when the capital became Hattusa. Hittite campaigns extended though Syria and Mesopotamia until the Hittite army ransacked Babylon in 1595 BC. Shortly after this the Hittite Kingdom was plunged into chaos and Syrian territories were was lost. The last monarch of the Old Kingdom, reigned until about 1500 BC and the following 70 years, the so-called Middle Kingdom has very sparse surviving records." ;
    skos:prefLabel "Old Hittite" ;
