<http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p08m57hdff8> a skos:Concept ;
    periodo:spatialCoverageDescription "Essex and Hertfordshire, parts of Kent, Suffolk, Cambridgeshire, Bedfordshire, Northamptonshire, Berkshire, Buckinghamshire and Oxfordshire" ;
    dcelements:language "en" ;
    dcterms:language <http://lexvo.org/id/iso639-1/en> ;
    owl:sameAs <http://collection.britishmuseum.org/id/thesauri/x114765> ;
    skos:altLabel "Eastern British Iron Age"@en ;
    skos:inScheme <http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p08m57h> ;
    skos:note "This term is restricted to Iron Age numismatics, and applies to coins produced between 80 BC-AD 50. It refers to an area roughly equivalent to modern Essex and Hertfordshire, parts of Kent, Suffolk, Cambridgeshire, Bedfordshire, Northamptonshire, Berkshire, Buckinghamshire and Oxfordshire, in which similar styled coinages are found. The various issuing authorities of this area seem to have relied on the same sources of technology and craftsmanship. Notable rulers in this area include Addedomaros, Dubnovellaunos, Tasciovanus, Dias, Rues and Cunobelin. The ethnic or tribal identities of these rulers and the anonymous issuers of earlier coins remain unclear, but some may have belonged to the Trinovantes or the Catuvellauni. Both are known from Roman sources describing the administrative structure of the later Roman province, but only the former definitely pre-dated the Roman invasion of AD 43. The term \"Northern\" was used by Hobbs in the BM catalogue (1996) but is often considered confusing.  J Creighton, Coins and Power in Iron Age Britain, Cambridge (CUP) 2000.  R Hobbs, British Iron Age Coins in the British Museum, London (BMP) 1996." ;
    skos:prefLabel "Eastern British Iron Age" ;
    time:intervalFinishedBy [ skos:prefLabel "AD 50" ;
            time:hasDateTimeDescription [ time:year "0050"^^xsd:gYear ] ] ;
    time:intervalStartedBy [ skos:prefLabel "80 BC" ;
            time:hasDateTimeDescription [ time:year "-0079"^^xsd:gYear ] ] ;
    foaf:page <http://collection.britishmuseum.org/id/thesauri/x114765> .

