        <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q399>,
        <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q43>,
        <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q483134>,
        <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q711>,
        <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q794>,
        <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q796>,
        <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q813>,
        <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q843>,
        <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q858>,
        <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q863>,
        <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q874>,
        <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q889> ;
    owl:sameAs <http://collection.britishmuseum.org/id/thesauri/x23190> ;
    skos:altLabel "Mongol"@en ;
    skos:inScheme <http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p08m57h> ;
    skos:note "1206-1370 (AH 602-AH 771). Rulers of Mongolia who conquered China, the 'Abbasid empire, the south Russian steppes and central Europe. The Mongol expansion took place under Genghis Khan in 1209 (AH 606). He took Beijing in 1215 (AH 612) thus controlling numerous commercial routes across central Asia to China. In 1220 (AH 616) Genghis Khan captured Bukhara and soon the whole of Transoxiana was part of the Mongol empire. In 1258 (AH 656) the Mongols sacked Baghdad under Hulegu grandson of Ghengis Khan and founder of the Il-Khanid dynasty (q.v.)." ;
    skos:prefLabel "Mongol" ;
    time:intervalFinishedBy [ skos:prefLabel "1370 (AH 771)" ;
            time:hasDateTimeDescription [ time:year "1370"^^xsd:gYear ] ] ;
    time:intervalStartedBy [ skos:prefLabel "1206 (AH 602)" ;
            time:hasDateTimeDescription [ time:year "1206"^^xsd:gYear ] ] ;
    foaf:page <http://collection.britishmuseum.org/id/thesauri/x23190> .

