    skos:note "The term applies to a group of peoples living in the region of Europe outside the Roman Empire known in classical sources as Germania, from around the 1st century BC - 8th century AD. During the Migration Period (around the late 4th-6th centuries AD) a number of them crossed the Rivers Rhine and Danube to settle within the former borders of the Empire." ;
