        <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q948> ;
    owl:sameAs <http://collection.britishmuseum.org/id/thesauri/x41025> ;
    skos:altLabel "Fatimid dynasty"@en ;
    skos:inScheme <http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p08m57h> ;
    skos:note "909-1171 (AH 297-AH 555). Rulers of North Africa, then Egypt and southern Syria who claimed title of caliph. They claimed descent from Fatima the daughter of the Prophet Mohammad and wife of the fourth Caliph 'Ali. In 909 (AH 297) the Mahdi was proclaimed caliph in rivalry to the 'Abbasids of Baghdad. From Egypt the Fatimids extended into Palestine and Syria and reached the zenith of their power in the 11th century." ;
    skos:prefLabel "Fatimid dynasty" ;
    time:intervalFinishedBy [ skos:prefLabel "1171 (AH 555)" ;
            time:hasDateTimeDescription [ time:year "1171"^^xsd:gYear ] ] ;
