    skos:altLabel "Salghurid dynasty"@en ;
    skos:inScheme <http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p08m57h> ;
    skos:note "1148-1282 (AH 543-AH 681). Ruled in Fars, southern Iran, as vassals of the Seljuqs and then in the 13th century as vassals of the Khwarazm Shahs and Mongols. They were of Turkmen origin. Sunqur was the founder of the Salghurids of Fars who consolidated his position in Persia when the power of the Great Seljuqs declined." ;
    skos:prefLabel "Salghurid dynasty" ;
    time:intervalFinishedBy [ skos:prefLabel "1282 (AH 681)" ;
