    skos:altLabel "Danishmandid dynasty"@en ;
    skos:inScheme <http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p08m57h> ;
    skos:note "1104-1178 (AH 497-AH 573). Turkman dynasty originally from north-central Anatolia and Cappadocia who controlled the northerly route of Turkmen access into Asia Minor. The name comes from Persian Danishmand meaning wise, learned man, scholar. In 1174 the line in Sivas was conquered by the Seljuqs of Rum, the line in Malatya and Elbistan fell to the Seljuqs of Rum in 1178." ;
    skos:prefLabel "Danishmandid dynasty" ;
    time:intervalFinishedBy [ skos:prefLabel "1178 (AH 573)" ;
