<http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p08m57hvrzw> a skos:Concept ;
    periodo:spatialCoverageDescription "classical Chorasmia on the lower Oxus" ;
    dcelements:language "en" ;
    dcterms:language <http://lexvo.org/id/iso639-1/en> ;
    dcterms:spatial <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q265>,
        <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q874>,
        <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q889> ;
    owl:sameAs <http://collection.britishmuseum.org/id/thesauri/x114378> ;
    skos:altLabel "Khwarazm Shahs"@en ;
    skos:inScheme <http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p08m57h> ;
    skos:note "995-1231 (AH 385-AH 628). Khwarazm is the classical Chorasmia, the rich and well irrigated region on the lower Oxus. In later times it was known as the Khanate of Khiva. It may have been an early home of the Iranians. Khwarazm was under Samanid rule until it was added to the Ghaznavid empire under Mahmud in 1017 (AH 408). After the middle of the 11th century Khwarazm was under Seljuq rule. Since the time of Malik Shah the hereditary governors of Khwarazm received the title of Khwarazm Shah. After the conquest of Transoxiana by Genghis Khan in 1220 (AH 617) Khwarazm came first under the rule of Mongols and then Turkish Central Asian steppe peoples." ;
    skos:prefLabel "Khwarazm Shahs" ;
    time:intervalFinishedBy [ skos:prefLabel "1231 (AH 628)" ;
            time:hasDateTimeDescription [ time:year "1231"^^xsd:gYear ] ] ;
    time:intervalStartedBy [ skos:prefLabel "995 (AH 385)" ;
            time:hasDateTimeDescription [ time:year "0995"^^xsd:gYear ] ] ;
    foaf:page <http://collection.britishmuseum.org/id/thesauri/x114378> .

