    skos:inScheme <http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p0b6j5m> ;
    skos:note "Broad designation derived from pottery chronology and from the stratigraphic history of the site (final period of occupation), independent of historical/art-historical periodization (hence the start at 1200 rather than with the Fourth Crusade and the capture of Constantinople in 1204). Used for the final phase of occupation in the South Region, which seems to have been destroyed before the end of the 13th century and largely abandoned." ;
    skos:prefLabel "13th century" ;
