    skos:altLabel "Early Nabatean Period"@en,
        "Hellenistic"@en ;
    skos:editorialNote "The early Nabatean coincides with the Hellenistic, so dates are derived from dating of the Hellenistic period in the chronological table on page 1529. This period does not refer to the Nabatean kingdom (first attested in 168 BCE and abolished by Romans in 106 CE), but rather Nabatean settlement and inhabitation. " ;
    skos:inScheme <http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p0dkm29> ;
    skos:note "\"Aretas I, the first known Nabatean ruler, is mentioned in 2 Maccabess 5:8. He is the Arabian prince from who the deposed High Priest Jason requested asylym in 168 BCE....Most of the Nabatean kings who reigned in Petra from that date until the abolishment of the Nabatean kingdom in 106 CE are known.\" (page 1181)" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Early Nabatean Period" ;
