    skos:editorialNote "The start date of 870 is a widely accepted but rough approximation of the settlement of Iceland." ;
    skos:inScheme <http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p0f66wq> ;
    skos:note "Traditionally, the Icelandic Age of Settlement is considered to have lasted from 874 to 930, at which point most of the island had been claimed and Alþingi (Althingi), the assembly of the Icelandic Commonwealth, was founded at Þingvellir (Thingvellir). (from https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Settlement_of_Iceland)." ;
