<http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p0j9r72hvmm> a skos:Concept ;
    periodo:spatialCoverageDescription "Greater Poland and Kujavy" ;
    dcelements:language "en" ;
    dcterms:language <http://lexvo.org/id/iso639-1/en> ;
    dcterms:source [ bibo:locator "20" ] ;
    dcterms:spatial <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q36> ;
    skos:altLabel "Brześć-Kujawski Culture IIIA"@en,
        "Late Band Pottery Culture IIIA"@en,
        "Late Lengyel IIIA"@en ;
    skos:broader <http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p0j9r7233z7> ;
    skos:editorialNote "For beginning of this phase, see ending of Late Lengyel IIB" ;
    skos:inScheme <http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p0j9r72> ;
    skos:note "\"Late Lengyel IIIA ended and Late Lengyel IIIB began in 4140–3975 CAL B .C. (95% probability; IIIA/IIIB) (FIG . 9), probably in 4085–4000 CAL B.C. (68% probability). Once more, this date estimate is compatible with the estimate for the equivalent transition at Racot 18, where it occurred in 4145–4050 CAL B.C. (95% probability; Racot IIIA/IIIB-1) (FIG . 10), probably in 4110–4060 CAL B.C. The dating of Late Lengyel IIIA is relatively robust, with seven assemblages associated with dates on short-life materials.\"" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Late Lengyel IIIA" ;
    time:intervalFinishedBy [ skos:prefLabel "-4085/-4000" ;
            time:hasDateTimeDescription [ periodo:earliestYear "-4085"^^xsd:gYear ;
                    periodo:latestYear "-4000"^^xsd:gYear ] ] ;
    time:intervalStartedBy [ skos:prefLabel "-4210/-4185" ;
            time:hasDateTimeDescription [ periodo:earliestYear "-4210"^^xsd:gYear ;
                    periodo:latestYear "-4185"^^xsd:gYear ] ] .

<http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p0j9r72pc85> a skos:Concept ;
    periodo:spatialCoverageDescription "Greater Poland and Kujavy" ;
    dcelements:language "en" ;
    dcterms:language <http://lexvo.org/id/iso639-1/en> ;
    dcterms:spatial <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q36> ;
    skos:altLabel "Breześć-Kujawski-Culture IIIB"@en,
        "Late Lengyel IIIB"@en ;
    skos:broader <http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p0j9r7233z7> ;
    skos:editorialNote "In this case the late end date is improbable as at that time, a number of other cultures have been attested. Therefore, the 68% range is given." ;
    skos:inScheme <http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p0j9r72> ;
    skos:note "\"Late Lengyel IIIA ended and Late Lengyel IIIB began in 4140–3975 CAL B .C. (95% probability; IIIA/IIIB) (FIG . 9), probably in 4085–4000 CAL B.C. (68% probability). Once more, this date estimate is compatible with the estimate for the equivalent transition at Racot 18, where it occurred in 4145–4050 CAL B.C. (95% probability; Racot IIIA/IIIB-1) (FIG . 10), probably in 4110–4060 CAL B.C. The dating of Late Lengyel IIIA is relatively robust, with seven assemblages associated with dates on short-life materials. The date when Late Lengyel IIIB ended is more uncertain, since we have only one assemblage associated with a short-life sample. The model suggests that Late Lengyel IIIB ended in 3905–2715 CAL B.C. (95% probability; end IIIB) (FIG. 9), probably in 3805–3370 CAL B.C. (68% probability). This is rather later than the end of Late Lengyel activity at Racot 18, which occurred in 4035–3990 CAL B.C. (95% probability; End Racot Late Lengyel) (FIG . 10), probably in 3970–3915 CAL B.C. (68% probability). It is currently not clear, however, whether Racot 18 ended before the demise of Late Lengyel IIIB ceramics elsewhere. Neither the animal bone from pit B354 at Bodzia 1 (Poz-43555) nor any of the dates on unidentified charcoal from this phase (FIG . 9) need be any later than the 40th century CAL B.C. Late Lengyel IIIB ceramics may continue later into the 4th millennium but, on present evidence, they need not have done so and, again, only further radiocarbon dates on short-life material associated with diagnostic cultural material will demonstrate this unequivocally." ;
    skos:prefLabel "Late Lengyel IIIB" ;
    time:intervalFinishedBy [ skos:prefLabel "-3805/-3370" ;
            time:hasDateTimeDescription [ periodo:earliestYear "-3805"^^xsd:gYear ;
                    periodo:latestYear "-3370"^^xsd:gYear ] ] ;
    time:intervalStartedBy [ skos:prefLabel "-4140/-3975 " ;
            time:hasDateTimeDescription [ periodo:earliestYear "-4140"^^xsd:gYear ;
                    periodo:latestYear "-3975"^^xsd:gYear ] ] .

<http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p0j9r72sbgb> a skos:Concept ;
    periodo:spatialCoverageDescription "Poland and Eastern Germany" ;
    dcelements:language "en" ;
    dcterms:language <http://lexvo.org/id/iso639-1/en> ;
    dcterms:source [ bibo:locator "18-19" ] ;
    dcterms:spatial <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q36> ;
    skos:altLabel "Stichbandkeramik"@de,
        "Late Band Pottery Culture I"@en,
        "Stroke Pottery Culture"@en ;
    skos:broader <http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p0j9r72g96p> ;
    skos:editorialNote "Late Band Pottery Culture (LBPC) I should not start before 4900 as at this time Linear Band Pottery is still attested. As there is only one 14C-date attached to the phasing, the given year dates are rounded to 100 to show imprecisions." ;
    skos:inScheme <http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p0j9r72> ;
    skos:note "\"LBPC I is estimated to have begun in 5585–4545 CAL B .C. (95% probability; start LBPC I) (FIG. 9), probably in 4940–4605 CAL B.C. (68% probability). The imprecision of this estimate accurately reflects that we have a single dated sample on short-life material from this phase (Gd-2509 on animal bone from pit 1 at Wegierce 12). The transition from LBPC I to LBPC IIA is estimated to have occurred in 4725–4530 CAL B .C. (95% probability; LBPC I/LBPC IIA) (FIG. 9), probably in 4760–4565 CAL B.C. (68% probability). On current evidence, we can thus say little more than that LBPC I ceramics in Poland probably date to some time within the first half of the 5th millennium CAL B .C., and that LBPC IIA ceramics probably appear in the century or two before 4500 CAL B.C.\"" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Late Band Pottery Culture I" ;
    time:intervalFinishedBy [ skos:prefLabel "-4700/-4500" ;
            time:hasDateTimeDescription [ periodo:earliestYear "-4700"^^xsd:gYear ;
                    periodo:latestYear "-4500"^^xsd:gYear ] ] ;
    time:intervalStartedBy [ skos:prefLabel "-4900/-4700" ;
            time:hasDateTimeDescription [ periodo:earliestYear "-4900"^^xsd:gYear ;
                    periodo:latestYear "-4700"^^xsd:gYear ] ] .

