    skos:editorialNote "This source updates the phasing proposed by the building's original excavators in Rostovtzeff, et al. 1939. As of its publication, it is considered the authoritative phasing for the Mithraeum. Note that this source, unlike Rostovtzeff, et al. 1939, decouples the phases of wall painting (Phase A, Phase B, Final Phase) from building construction phases (Mithraeum I, Mithraeum II)." ;
    skos:inScheme <http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p0mx5nb> ;
    skos:note "One of at least two wall painting phases belonging to Mithraeum I; authors note that phases of wall decoration and structural changes to buildings do not always correspond to the same moment of intervention (169, 176). Note 33 to p. 169: \"If the final decoration is dated to 209/10, the other two phases are perhaps to be dated to around 200 and 180 CE respectively.\"" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Phase B" ;
    time:intervalFinishedBy [ skos:prefLabel "209/10 CE" ;
            time:hasDateTimeDescription [ periodo:earliestYear "0209"^^xsd:gYear ;
                    periodo:latestYear "0210"^^xsd:gYear ] ] ;
    time:intervalStartedBy [ skos:prefLabel "around 200 CE" ;
            time:hasDateTimeDescription [ time:year "0200"^^xsd:gYear ] ] .

