<http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p0rc4w75rs7> a skos:Concept ;
    periodo:spatialCoverageDescription "Udhruh (Southern Jordan)" ;
    dcelements:language "en" ;
    dcterms:language <http://lexvo.org/id/iso639-1/en> ;
    dcterms:spatial <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q810> ;
    skos:altLabel "Nabatean Period"@en ;
    skos:editorialNote """Start dates are derived from earliest attested presence of Nabateans and the latest agreed-upon possible date. End date is derived from the beginning of the Roman period.

Author mentions a Hellenistic period in connection to the Nabatean period but omits any distinct period of Greek/Hellenistic dominance in the chronology. """ ;
    skos:inScheme <http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p0rc4w7> ;
    skos:note """"The Nabataean presence in southern Jordan is indisputably attested in the accounts of Greek and Roman sources as early as 312 B.C." (page 9) 

"It is commonly agreed that by the first century B.C. at least, Nabateans had permanent settlements in Edom and throughout most of modern Jordan." (page 201) 

"The rest of the country will have remained under the Nabataean control, as part of their kingdom, until AD 106 when Trajan's troops subdued Petra and what was a Nabataean realm became the Roman province of Arabia." (page 208)

"Thus, the size and number of sites occupied during the Nabataean period in the study area is significant, specially when compared with previous settlements, and after the tangible gap in human settlement through the Persian and Hellenistic periods." (page 202)""" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Nabatean Period" ;
    time:intervalFinishedBy [ skos:prefLabel "AD 106 " ;
            time:hasDateTimeDescription [ time:year "0106"^^xsd:gYear ] ] ;
    time:intervalStartedBy [ skos:prefLabel "by the first century B.C." ;
            time:hasDateTimeDescription [ periodo:earliestYear "-0311"^^xsd:gYear ;
                    periodo:latestYear "-0099"^^xsd:gYear ] ] .

<http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p0rc4w75sr6> a skos:Concept ;
