        <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q963> ;
    skos:altLabel "Mosselbaai"@af,
        "Klasies MSA II"@en,
        "Klasies Middle Stone Age II"@en,
        "MSA 2b"@en,
        "Middle Stone Age 2b"@en,
        "Mossel Bay"@en,
        "Mossel Bay phase"@en,
        "Volman MSA 2b"@en,
        "Volman Middle Stone Age 2b"@en ;
    skos:broader <http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p0s2rwknqbf> ;
    skos:inScheme <http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p0s2rwk> ;
    skos:note """Triangular points with convergent flakes (Goodwin and van Riet Lowe 1929), Wurz uses term for pre-Still Bay of Klasies River.

The Mossel Bay lithic industry is characterized by bifacial points, sometimes used as a synonym for Still Bay. The minimum and maximum ages are estimated based on Lombard et al. 2012. See Keller 1970 (SAAB) for description.

Alternate labels based on Wurz S, 2002. Variability in the Middle Stone Age Lithic Sequence, 115,000–60,000 Years Ago at Klasies River, South Africa. Journal of Archaeological Science 29, 1001–1015.""" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Mossel Bay" ;
