<http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p0s2rwk8vhh> a skos:Concept ;
    periodo:spatialCoverageDescription "Central Africa" ;
    dcelements:language "en" ;
    dcterms:language <http://lexvo.org/id/iso639-1/en> ;
    dcterms:spatial <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q1000>,
        <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q1009>,
        <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q657>,
        <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q929>,
        <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q971>,
        <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q974>,
        <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q983> ;
    skos:altLabel "Karari Industry"@en ;
    skos:broader <http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p0s2rwknm9c> ;
    skos:inScheme <http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p0s2rwk> ;
    skos:note """Similar to Developed Oldowan, with a conspicuous incidence of core scrapers.

The formal category Karari Industry has been proposed to designate assemblages from the Lower Okote Member. This industry displays a rather loose, heterogeneous set of characteristics. Assemblages exemplifying these characteristics are to be understood as a facies of variable sets of toolkits. This industry shares broad, generalized features with near-contemporary industries such as the Developed Oldowan A from Bed II at Olduvai, but also show distinctive patterns of difference.""" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Karari Industry" ;
    time:intervalFinishedBy [ skos:prefLabel "1400000 BP2000" ;
            time:hasDateTimeDescription [ time:year "-1398000"^^xsd:gYear ] ] ;
    time:intervalStartedBy [ skos:prefLabel "1600000 BP2000" ;
            time:hasDateTimeDescription [ time:year "-1598000"^^xsd:gYear ] ] .

