<http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p0s2rwkd4n5> a skos:Concept ;
    periodo:spatialCoverageDescription "Levant" ;
    dcelements:language "en" ;
    dcterms:language <http://lexvo.org/id/iso639-1/en> ;
    dcterms:spatial <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q81483> ;
    skos:altLabel "Harifian"@en ;
    skos:broader <http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p0s2rwks8k2> ;
    skos:inScheme <http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p0s2rwk> ;
    skos:note """Harif point, obliquely truncated bladelet with pointed base formed by microburin technique and steep retouch. Summary: Microburin technique used habitually on large sites, absent in small inventories, Harif points, small lunates and triangles, Mostly simple backing, Helwan retouch very rare, Round houses.

Found in desert southern Levant, Negev and Sinai, contemporaneous with late Natufian of northern parts of the Levant (Goring-Morris 1987, 257, Schyle & Uerpmann 1996, 268). Harifian hunter-gatherer culture in seasonal camps defined at Abu Salem in Central Negev (Marks & Scott 1976), discovered 1969 around the plateau of Tar Harif.""" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Harifian" ;
    time:intervalFinishedBy [ skos:prefLabel "11000 BP2000" ;
            time:hasDateTimeDescription [ time:year "-9000"^^xsd:gYear ] ] ;
    time:intervalStartedBy [ skos:prefLabel "14000 BP2000" ;
            time:hasDateTimeDescription [ time:year "-12000"^^xsd:gYear ] ] .

