<http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p0s2rwkdv6q> a skos:Concept ;
    periodo:spatialCoverageDescription "Eurasia" ;
    dcelements:language "en" ;
    dcterms:language <http://lexvo.org/id/iso639-1/en> ;
    dcterms:spatial <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q46>,
        <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q48> ;
    skos:altLabel "Tayacian"@en ;
    skos:inScheme <http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p0s2rwk> ;
    skos:note """Equivalent to Tabun F-type in Israel.

Obsolete techno-complex, use Late Acheulean - Levant, age range probably narrower. Sometimes used to describe Low and Mid Paleolithic flake industries lacking handaxes, bifaces and retouched pieces. Originally used for industries from lower levels at La Micoque, subsequently applied to industries over wide geographical and chronol range. Layers belonging to penultimate glacial period assigned to Tayacian. Also describes primitive flake-tool tradition of Israel, like smaller Clactonian industry.""" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Tayacian" ;
    time:intervalFinishedBy [ skos:prefLabel "250000 BP2000" ;
            time:hasDateTimeDescription [ time:year "-248000"^^xsd:gYear ] ] ;
    time:intervalStartedBy [ skos:prefLabel "700000 BP2000" ;
            time:hasDateTimeDescription [ time:year "-698000"^^xsd:gYear ] ] .

<http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p0s2rwkdztt> a skos:Concept ;
    periodo:spatialCoverageDescription "Southern Africa" ;
    dcelements:language "en" ;
    dcterms:language <http://lexvo.org/id/iso639-1/en> ;
    dcterms:spatial <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q1013>,
