<http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p0s2rwkjpgp> a skos:Concept ;
    periodo:spatialCoverageDescription "East Asia" ;
    dcelements:language "en" ;
    dcterms:language <http://lexvo.org/id/iso639-1/en> ;
    dcterms:spatial <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q148>,
        <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q17>,
        <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q483134>,
        <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q865> ;
    skos:altLabel "Middle Paleolithic"@en,
        "Middle Paleolithic - E Asia"@en ;
    skos:broader <http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p0s2rwkt9hw> ;
    skos:inScheme <http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p0s2rwk> ;
    skos:note """In general, MP finds are made of poor quality local raw material, using direct-hard hammer percussion without preparing cores. Regular flakes often used as they are, but some shaped regular tools, mainly side scrapers are present. Technology is often simple free-hand core reduction or bipolar technique. Some diversity does exist, as shown by the Huangniliang site in NE China.

The Middle Paleolithic in China is also referred to as later Early Paleolithic and Late Paleolithic.""" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Middle Paleolithic" ;
    time:intervalFinishedBy [ skos:prefLabel "35000 BP2000" ;
