<http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p0s2rwkn79h> a skos:Concept ;
    periodo:spatialCoverageDescription "Levant" ;
    dcelements:language "en" ;
    dcterms:language <http://lexvo.org/id/iso639-1/en> ;
    dcterms:spatial <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q81483> ;
    skos:altLabel "Nizzanian"@en ;
    skos:broader <http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p0s2rwks8k2> ;
    skos:inScheme <http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p0s2rwk> ;
    skos:note """Assemblages are characterized by small triangular microliths, and gravette and microgravette points. Further finds include beautiful end scrapers and dihedral burins. The microburin technique is used habitually. Summary: Habitual use of the microburin technique, Small triangular microliths, gravette points and microgravettes.

Sites of the Nizzanian are often grouped into older phases of Geometric Kebaran dating to 17-15 ka BP and contemporary with later Kebaran. First sites described are Wadi Jilat 6 and Ein Gev IV (Bar-Yosef 1980, 1981). Newer finds have expanded the distribution of the Nizzanian from the Negev and the coastal plains to the Azraq Basin (Garrard 1998). Sites vary considerably in size, from huge expanses in Wadi Jilat 6 and Karaneh IV, to smaller sizes and ephemeral camps.""" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Nizzanian" ;
    time:intervalFinishedBy [ skos:prefLabel "16000 BP2000" ;
            time:hasDateTimeDescription [ time:year "-14000"^^xsd:gYear ] ] ;
    time:intervalStartedBy [ skos:prefLabel "18000 BP2000" ;
            time:hasDateTimeDescription [ time:year "-16000"^^xsd:gYear ] ] .

<http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p0s2rwkn8cc> a skos:Concept ;
