<http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p0s2rwknq95> a skos:Concept ;
    periodo:spatialCoverageDescription "Levant" ;
    dcelements:language "en" ;
    dcterms:language <http://lexvo.org/id/iso639-1/en> ;
    dcterms:spatial <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q81483> ;
    skos:altLabel "Mushabian"@en ;
    skos:broader <http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p0s2rwks8k2> ;
    skos:inScheme <http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p0s2rwk> ;
    skos:note """Classic Mushabian characterized by dominance of arch-backed bladelets, La Mouillah points and scalene triangles, all truncated at one end using microburin technique. Helwan lunates also included. Rectangular and trapezoidal microliths mostly absent. Some assemblages contain Ramon points, similar to La Mouillah points. Summary: Microburin technique, Arch-backed bladelets and scalene triangles, La Mouillah points, all truncated at one end using microburin technique.

The Mushabian was found in southern Jordan, Negev and Sinai and can be divided into an earlier phase (14,500-12,800 BP) of a classical Mushabian and a later phase with the finds from Shunera (Goring-Morris 1987) which overlaps with the Early Natufian (12,800-11,000 BP). It was first discovered during excavations in the northern Sinai in the 1970s (Phillips & Mintz 1977).""" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Mushabian" ;
    time:intervalFinishedBy [ skos:prefLabel "14000 BP2000" ;
            time:hasDateTimeDescription [ time:year "-12000"^^xsd:gYear ] ] ;
    time:intervalStartedBy [ skos:prefLabel "16000 BP2000" ;
            time:hasDateTimeDescription [ time:year "-14000"^^xsd:gYear ] ] .

