<http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p0s2rwkpzxh> a skos:Concept ;
    periodo:spatialCoverageDescription "Eurasia" ;
    dcelements:language "en" ;
    dcterms:language <http://lexvo.org/id/iso639-1/en> ;
    dcterms:spatial <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q46> ;
    skos:altLabel "Epigravettian"@en ;
    skos:broader <http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p0s2rwks8k2> ;
    skos:editorialNote "Coverage changed from \"Europe\" to \"Eurasia\" as of June 2024." ;
    skos:inScheme <http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p0s2rwk> ;
    skos:note """The Epigravettian technocomplex is well known in southern and eastern Europe and dates right after the Gravettian. Its material culture is similar to the Gravettian with the use of fine blades, bladelets, and, in many cases, microblades to manufacture backed tools. Bone tools, art, and symbolic artifacts, mostly representing animals and geometric motives, are also very common.

One site in Armenia, Kalavan-1, is attributed to the Epigravettian, but to date, no Gravettian sites are known from the Caucasus. If it is true it is the southeastern-most occurrence of the Epigravettian.""" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Epigravettian" ;
    time:intervalFinishedBy [ skos:prefLabel "10000 BP2000" ;
            time:hasDateTimeDescription [ time:year "-8000"^^xsd:gYear ] ] ;
    time:intervalStartedBy [ skos:prefLabel "21000 BP2000" ;
            time:hasDateTimeDescription [ time:year "-19000"^^xsd:gYear ] ] .

