<http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p0s2rwkrm8q> a skos:Concept ;
    periodo:spatialCoverageDescription "Levant" ;
    dcelements:language "en" ;
    dcterms:language <http://lexvo.org/id/iso639-1/en> ;
    skos:altLabel "Kebaran"@en ;
    skos:broader <http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p0s2rwks8k2> ;
    skos:inScheme <http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p0s2rwk> ;
    skos:note """Simple, lacks complexity and abundance of forms compared to later industries. Differences fluid, assemblages dominated by micropoints (curved backed bladelets with wider base), backed points, obliquely truncated backed bladelets, micropoints, or other backed pieces. Summary: No habitual use of the microburin technique, Mostly non-geometric microliths, First industry with invasive retouch/backing of the pieces, Two large phases, with the later phase yielding truncated pieces.

Dates about 20-14 ka uncal BP Fellner (1995a, 22). A widespread phenomenon in the Mediterranean zone and oases of Palestine, Israel, southern Syria, Lebanon and western Jordan, extending into the desert areas of the Negev and Sinai. The desert areas seem to have been settled slightly later, with dates of about 16 ka uncal BP.""" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Kebaran" ;
    time:intervalFinishedBy [ skos:prefLabel "18000 BP2000" ;
            time:hasDateTimeDescription [ time:year "-16000"^^xsd:gYear ] ] ;
    time:intervalStartedBy [ skos:prefLabel "22000 BP2000" ;
            time:hasDateTimeDescription [ time:year "-20000"^^xsd:gYear ] ] .

