<http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p0s2rwkw38q> a skos:Concept ;
    periodo:spatialCoverageDescription "Levant" ;
    dcelements:language "en" ;
    dcterms:language <http://lexvo.org/id/iso639-1/en> ;
    dcterms:spatial <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q81483> ;
    skos:altLabel "Geometric Kebaran"@en ;
    skos:broader <http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p0s2rwks8k2> ;
    skos:inScheme <http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p0s2rwk> ;
    skos:note """Lithics consist of laminar debitage and microliths, >50% rectangular and trapezoidal forms. Addition of 2nd truncation on Geometric Kebaran blanks, resulting in rectangular microliths unlike truncated pieces of Kebaran. Summary: No habitual use of microburin technique, geometric microliths, Mostly rectangular and trapezoidal forms, Rare occurrence of Helwan retouch, Regular finds of shell beads and ornaments.

Geometric Kebaran or Kebaran A dates 14,500-12,500 BP from southern Sinai to Syria. Older sites are found on the coast and may correlate with dry conditions of the LGM. During more humid conditions until the Geometric Kebaran expanded further inland, ending ca. 13,000 BP before the early Natufian climatic deterioration. Finds from the north in the El Kowm Basin of Syria are quite similar to those from southern Sinai.""" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Geometric Kebaran" ;
    time:intervalFinishedBy [ skos:prefLabel "14000 BP2000" ;
            time:hasDateTimeDescription [ time:year "-12000"^^xsd:gYear ] ] ;
    time:intervalStartedBy [ skos:prefLabel "17000 BP2000" ;
            time:hasDateTimeDescription [ time:year "-15000"^^xsd:gYear ] ] .

