    skos:altLabel "Early period (northern Roman Noricum)"@en,
        "Frühzeit (römisches Nordnoricum)"@en ;
    skos:broader <http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p0s84tq2ndm> ;
    skos:editorialNote "While the early Roman period for southern Noricum started earlier (cf. Hagmann 2021, <http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p0ndpcqbmxk>), due to the historical development, a significant establishment of a Roman settlement in the Danubian area (which corresponds to northern Noricum) can only be expected around or after AD 50 (cf., Hagmann, Dominik, 2022. A \"Roman Rural Landscape\" in Northeastern Noricum: Results of Landscape Archaeological Investigations on Rural Settlement of the Roman Imperial Period in Lower Austria. In Franz Pieler/Wolfgang Breibert (eds.), Contributions to the Lower Austrian Regional Archaeology Day 2022, pp. 61-70. Scientific Publications from the Regional Collections of Lower Austria Asparn/Zaya, <https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.6751583>)." ;
