<http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p0znh3t4t68> a skos:Concept ;
    dcelements:language "en" ;
    dcterms:language <http://lexvo.org/id/iso639-1/en> ;
    dcterms:spatial <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q38>,
        <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q41> ;
    skos:altLabel "Florid Style"@en ;
    skos:editorialNote "It is unclear whether the author means the lifespan or reign of Pyrrhus in his description. I have therefore inferred a Start and Stop date from Pyrrhus' lifespan (the broader range). cf. https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pyrrhus_of_Epirus#cite_note-1" ;
    skos:inScheme <http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p0znh3t> ;
    skos:note "p. 288-290: \"It is by no means necessary to suppose that one style of fabric ceased immediately on the introduction of another and improved one; on the contrary, it probably continued till so entirely superseded that the fabric became obsolete. Hence the transition from the 'fine' style of the earlier vases to a subsequent one, which may be termed florid--analogous to the state of art in the time of Pyrrhus.\"" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Florid Style" ;
    time:intervalFinishedBy [ skos:prefLabel "Time of Pyrrhus" ;
            time:hasDateTimeDescription [ time:year "-0271"^^xsd:gYear ] ] ;
    time:intervalStartedBy [ skos:prefLabel "Time of Pyrrhus" ;
            time:hasDateTimeDescription [ time:year "-0318"^^xsd:gYear ] ] .

<http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p0znh3t5s5w> a skos:Concept ;
    dcelements:language "en" ;
    dcterms:language <http://lexvo.org/id/iso639-1/en> ;
    dcterms:source [ dcterms:isPartOf <http://www.worldcat.org/oclc/1358252> ;
            bibo:locator "285, 290" ] ;
    dcterms:spatial <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q38>,
        <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q41> ;
    skos:altLabel "Fine Style"@en ;
    skos:editorialNote """Author apparently miscalculates Start date as "Ol. XCIV, B.C. 403". The 94th Olympiad would range from 400 to 396 BC (ISO values: -399 to -395). I have opted to use his more precise dating of "B.C. 403" as a precise Start.

It is unclear whether author indicates the lifespan or the reign of Pyrrhus when indicating "the time of Pyrrhus" as the period in which the florid style gradually replaced the fine style. I have therefore opted for the wider range (Pyrrhus' life) to infer an earliest and latest stop. cf. https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pyrrhus_of_Epirus#cite_note-1""" ;
    skos:inScheme <http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p0znh3t> ;
    skos:note """p.285: "The age of these vases is fixed by the appearance of the long vowels, the changed form of the aspirate, and the presence of the double or aspirated letters, introduced into the public acts after the archonship of Euclid, Olympiad XCIV., B.C. 403."

p.288-90: "It is by no means necessary to suppose that one style of fabric ceased immediately on the introduction of another and improved one; on the contrary, it probably continued till so entirely superseded that the fabric became obsolete. Hence the transition from the 'fine' style of the earlier vases to a subsequent one, which may be termed florid -- analogous to the state of art in the time of Pyrrhus.\"""" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Fine Style" ;
    time:intervalFinishedBy [ skos:prefLabel "Time of Pyrrhus" ;
            time:hasDateTimeDescription [ periodo:earliestYear "-0318"^^xsd:gYear ;
                    periodo:latestYear "-0271"^^xsd:gYear ] ] ;
    time:intervalStartedBy [ skos:prefLabel "B.C. 403" ;
            time:hasDateTimeDescription [ time:year "-0402"^^xsd:gYear ] ] .

<http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p0znh3tjnv8> a skos:Concept ;
    dcelements:language "en" ;
    dcterms:language <http://lexvo.org/id/iso639-1/en> ;
    dcterms:source [ dcterms:isPartOf <http://www.worldcat.org/oclc/1358252> ;
            bibo:locator "282" ] ;
    dcterms:spatial <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q38>,
        <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q41> ;
    skos:altLabel "Strong Style"@en ;
    skos:inScheme <http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p0znh3t> ;
    skos:note """p. 282: "The age of these vases is placed between the L. and LXXX. Olympiads. Recent discoveries have shown that vases of this style are as old as the Parthenon, destroyed by the Persians, Ol. LXXV., B.C. 480, and certainly prior to the age of Pheidias. [see note 3] The vases with the historical subjects of Alcaeus, Ol. XLII., B.C. 612; Anacreon, Ol. LV., B.C. 560; and Croesus, Ol. LVIII., B.C. 548, are in this style. The alphabet resembles that which appears in the Athenian inscriptions of Ol. LXXXVI., B.C. 436, but the language is both Attic and Doric."

p.282 n.3: "Jahn, Vasensammlung, s. clxxiv. clxxv; Allg. Monatsschr, 1852, p. 356.\"""" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Strong Style" ;
    time:intervalFinishedBy [ skos:prefLabel "LXXX. Olympiad" ;
            time:hasDateTimeDescription [ periodo:earliestYear "-0455"^^xsd:gYear ;
                    periodo:latestYear "-0451"^^xsd:gYear ] ] ;
    time:intervalStartedBy [ skos:prefLabel "L. Olympiad" ;
            time:hasDateTimeDescription [ periodo:earliestYear "-0575"^^xsd:gYear ;
                    periodo:latestYear "-0571"^^xsd:gYear ] ] .

<http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p0znh3tjqgh> a skos:Concept ;
    dcelements:language "en" ;
    dcterms:language <http://lexvo.org/id/iso639-1/en> ;
