    skos:altLabel "Mithraeum II"@en ;
    skos:editorialNote "This source updates the phasing proposed by the building's original excavators in Rostovtzeff, et al. 1939. As of its publication, it is considered the authoritative phasing for the Mithraeum. Note that this source, unlike Rostovtzeff, et al. 1939, decouples the phases of wall painting (Phase A, Phase B, Final Phase) from building construction phases (Mithraeum I, Mithraeum II)." ;
    skos:inScheme <http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p0mx5nb> ;
    skos:note "Start of Mithraeum II building phase determined by the inscription referring to the rebuilding of a temple to mithras under Antonius Valentinus (CIMRM 1.53; AE 1940.220; PR VII + VIII no. 847, p. 85), found in the fill above the mithraeum (p. 167, 176); end of phase determined by construction of the seige rampart in wall street c. 256 CE (p. 165)." ;
    skos:prefLabel "Mithraeum II" ;
    time:intervalFinishedBy [ skos:prefLabel "256 CE" ;
            time:hasDateTimeDescription [ time:year "0256"^^xsd:gYear ] ] ;
    time:intervalStartedBy [ skos:prefLabel "209-211 CE" ;
            time:hasDateTimeDescription [ periodo:earliestYear "0209"^^xsd:gYear ;
                    periodo:latestYear "0211"^^xsd:gYear ] ] ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p0pkpgk57tt>,
        <http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p0pkpgkwxn7> .

<http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p0ndpcqhj2r> a skos:Concept ;
    periodo:spatialCoverageDescription "Donauprovinzen" ;
    dcelements:language "de" ;
    dcterms:language <http://lexvo.org/id/iso639-1/de> ;
    dcterms:source [ bibo:locator "370" ] ;
    dcterms:spatial <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q40> ;
    skos:altLabel "Die Zeit der Severer"@de,
        "Severan period"@en ;
    skos:broader <http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p0ndpcqvh8h> ;
    skos:editorialNote "\"Gassner, Verena; Jilek, Sonja; Ladstätter, Sabine (2002–2003): Am Rande des Reiches. Die Römer in Österreich. Österreichische Geschichte 15 v. Chr.–378 n. Chr. Vienna: Ueberreuter. <http://www.worldcat.org/oclc/780936246>\" is one of the most important contributions which still represents the most comprehensive account of the Roman period's archaeology for the former Roman provinces on the territory of present-day Austria. This is especially true for the holistic presentation of all aspects of archaeology concerning the province of Noricum." ;
    skos:inScheme <http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p0ndpcq> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Die Zeit der Severer" ;
    time:intervalFinishedBy [ skos:prefLabel "AD 235" ;
            time:hasDateTimeDescription [ time:year "0235"^^xsd:gYear ] ] ;
    time:intervalStartedBy [ skos:prefLabel "AD 193" ;
            time:hasDateTimeDescription [ time:year "0193"^^xsd:gYear ] ] .

<http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p0ndpcqmz45> a skos:Concept ;
    periodo:spatialCoverageDescription "Donauprovinzen" ;
    dcelements:language "de" ;
    dcterms:language <http://lexvo.org/id/iso639-1/de> ;
    dcterms:source [ bibo:locator "70. 369" ] ;
    dcterms:spatial <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q40> ;
    skos:altLabel "römisches Emporium auf dem Magdalensberg"@de,
        "Roman emporium on Magdalensberg mountain"@en ;
    skos:broader <http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p0ndpcqvjj5> ;
    skos:editorialNote """The settlement on the Magdalensberg belongs to several pre-Roman and Roman phases of Roman Noricum's early history because this settlement has been an emporium/outpost before Roman occupation in pre-Roman times (around 50 BC) and the only one of its kind. Between 15 BC and AD 41 the settlement on the Magdalensberg has been the center of Roman administration of Noricum. Finally, the settlement activities stopped shortly before AD 50 in parallel to establishing the province and the foundation of several cities, which happened around AD 41. This site is essential for the archeological finds, contexts, and chronology and, therefore, the history of the province's early phase; for a discussion cf. e.g., Gleirscher, Paul (2009). Zur antiken Bebauung auf dem Gipfel des Magdalensbergs: Zwischen Oppidum, Königsburg und Heiligtum. Bonner Jahrbücher 207, 103–120. <https://doi.org/10.11588/bjb.2007.0.33144>

Source of the period: "Gassner, Verena; Jilek, Sonja; Ladstätter, Sabine (2002–2003): Am Rande des Reiches. Die Römer in Österreich. Österreichische Geschichte 15 v. Chr.–378 n. Chr. Vienna: Ueberreuter. <http://www.worldcat.org/oclc/780936246>" is one of the most important contributions which still represents the most comprehensive account of the Roman period's archaeology for the former Roman provinces on the territory of present-day Austria. This is especially true for the holistic presentation of all aspects of archaeology concerning the province of Noricum.""" ;
    skos:inScheme <http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p0ndpcq> ;
    skos:note "Settlement activities on the Magdalensberg mountain ended shortly before the mid of the 1st century AD: \"Der Zeitpunkt der Auflassung wird anhand der Funde noch vor der Mitte des 1. Jahrhunderts n. Chr. angesetzt, danach bricht der Zustrom an Importen jäh ab.\" – p. 70." ;
    skos:prefLabel "römisches Emporium auf dem Magdalensberg" ;
    time:intervalFinishedBy [ skos:prefLabel "noch vor der Mitte des 1. Jahrhunderts n. Chr." ;
            time:hasDateTimeDescription [ periodo:earliestYear "0040"^^xsd:gYear ;
                    periodo:latestYear "0050"^^xsd:gYear ] ] ;
    time:intervalStartedBy [ skos:prefLabel "c. 50 BC" ;
            time:hasDateTimeDescription [ time:year "-0049"^^xsd:gYear ] ] .

