    skos:editorialNote "The period describes the whole timespan of Roman interactions, specifically for northern Roman Noricum, which corresponds to the Danube region. The period contains the overarching periods defined for northern Roman Noricum (\"Early Period (northern Roman Noricum),\" \"Imperial Period,\" and \"Late Antiquity\"; derived from Hagmann 2021, <http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p0s84tq>). While the early Roman period for southern Noricum started earlier (cf. Hagmann 2021, <http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p0ndpcqbmxk>), due to the historical development, a significant establishment of a Roman settlement in the Danubian area (which corresponds to northern Noricum) can only be expected around or after AD 50 (cf., Hagmann, Dominik, 2022. A \"Roman Rural Landscape\" in Northeastern Noricum: Results of Landscape Archaeological Investigations on Rural Settlement of the Roman Imperial Period in Lower Austria. In Franz Pieler/Wolfgang Breibert (eds.), Contributions to the Lower Austrian Regional Archaeology Day 2022, pp. 61-70. Scientific Publications from the Regional Collections of Lower Austria Asparn/Zaya, <https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.6751583>). Furthermore, in addition to the absolute early period, the highly late period between 488 and 500 AD is also considered, in the context of which, according to \"classical\" doctrine and in view of the written tradition (vita Sancti Severini), 488 AD a settlement of the remaining Roman population (so-called \"Romanen\" in German-speaking research) should have already taken place and which represents a historically highly ambiguous period during the transition to the early Middle Ages (cf., Eichert - Richards 2022, <http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p0cwwzn>)." ;
    skos:inScheme <http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p0s84tq> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Roman antiquity (northern Roman Noricum)" ;
    time:intervalFinishedBy [ skos:prefLabel "500 AD" ;
            time:hasDateTimeDescription [ time:year "0500"^^xsd:gYear ] ] ;
    time:intervalStartedBy [ skos:prefLabel "50 AD" ;
            time:hasDateTimeDescription [ time:year "0050"^^xsd:gYear ] ] ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p0cwwznw938>,
        <http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p0ndpcqn83v>,
        <http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p0s84tq9w22> ;
    foaf:page <http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p0s84tq> .

<http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p0t35856b5j> a skos:Concept ;
    periodo:spatialCoverageDescription "Central Texas" ;
    dcelements:language "en" ;
    dcterms:language <http://lexvo.org/id/iso639-1/en> ;
    dcterms:source [ bibo:locator "p. 5, fig. 2; p. 20; p. 24" ] ;
    dcterms:spatial <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q1439> ;
    skos:altLabel "Early Archaic Period"@en ;
    skos:broader <http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p0t3585kxnj> ;
    skos:editorialNote "End date for period taken from chart on p. 5 and from start date of following period." ;
    skos:inScheme <http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p0t3585> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Early Archaic Period" ;
    time:intervalFinishedBy [ skos:prefLabel "around 3600 B.C." ;
