<http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p0t3585fjns> a skos:Concept ;
    periodo:spatialCoverageDescription "Central Texas" ;
    dcelements:language "en" ;
    dcterms:language <http://lexvo.org/id/iso639-1/en> ;
    dcterms:source [ bibo:locator "p. 5, fig. 2; p. 18; pp. 39-41" ] ;
    dcterms:spatial <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q1439> ;
    skos:altLabel "Late Prehistoric period"@en,
        "Neo-American period"@en,
        "Neoarchaic period"@en,
        "Neoindian period"@en ;
    skos:editorialNote "While the author indicates that the Late Archaic period ends around A.D. 600 in the chart on p. 5 and in the text on p. 39, the subsequent expressions about alternatives and uncertainties are represented by the A.D. 400-1200 range. The author indicates a preference for the label \"Post-Archaic\" on p. 18, where it is attributed to Prewitt in an unpublished report, but all of the cited works by Prewitt in fact use \"Neoarchaic\"." ;
    skos:inScheme <http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p0t3585> ;
    skos:note "\"I provisionally stop the Late Archaic period around A.D. 600...Nevertheless, one should underscore the fact that some cultural and considerable economic continuity tied the end of the Late Archaic period with what came directly afterwards. In fact, of all the period boundaries set in the present paper, that for the ending of the Late Archaic II subperiod is the most subjective and bothersome. For one thing, human culture did not change greatly after the beginning of that interval down through the days when Scallorn arrowheads were in vogue. If the informed reader wishes to terminate the Late Archaic period at A.D. 1200, I will not argue. Or if the reader wants to stop the period at around A.D. 400 (or later), when very small \"dart\" points of the Darl and Figueroa sort appear in the region, that is another possibility\" (pp. 39-40). \"The present historical narrative concludes at A.D. 1600, near the end of Toyah days when Perdiz arrowheads were in vogue\" (p. 41)." ;
    skos:prefLabel "Post-Archaic Era" ;
    time:intervalFinishedBy [ skos:prefLabel "A.D. 1600" ;
            time:hasDateTimeDescription [ time:year "1600"^^xsd:gYear ] ] ;
    time:intervalStartedBy [ skos:prefLabel "A.D. 400/A.D. 1200" ;
            time:hasDateTimeDescription [ periodo:earliestYear "0400"^^xsd:gYear ;
                    periodo:latestYear "1200"^^xsd:gYear ] ] ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p0qkjhb4hmc> .

