<http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p0nt759mt2t> a skos:Concept ;
    periodo:spatialCoverageDescription "Tauric Chersonesos" ;
    dcelements:language "ru" ;
    dcterms:language <http://lexvo.org/id/iso639-1/ru> ;
    dcterms:source [ bibo:locator "http://chersonesos.org/?p=history_ant#10" ] ;
    skos:altLabel "Late Antiquity"@en ;
    skos:editorialNote "The spatial coverage of this period extends to the site of Tauric Chersonesos (https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/226564) in Crimea, but spatial coverage area cannot be specified because Crimea is currently considered occupied territory by the international community (Ukrainian sovereignty, Russian control)." ;
    skos:inScheme <http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p0nt759> ;
    skos:note """"В третьей четверти III в. начинается заключительный этап римского периода в истории Херсонеса, который иногда рассматривают в качестве самостоятельного и называют позднеантичным. Его начало относится к третьей четверти III, а конец - ко второй четверти - середине VI в."

English version: "The third quarter of the 3rd century AD marked the final stage of the Roman period in the history of Chersonesos, a period which is sometimes considered a separate phase and called Late Antiquity. It begins in the third quarter of the 3rd century AD and ends in the mid-third quarter of the 6th century AD.\"""" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Позднеантичный" ;
    time:intervalFinishedBy [ skos:prefLabel "второй четверти - середине VI в" ;
            time:hasDateTimeDescription [ periodo:earliestYear "0525"^^xsd:gYear ;
                    periodo:latestYear "0575"^^xsd:gYear ] ] ;
    time:intervalStartedBy [ skos:prefLabel "третьей четверти III в" ;
            time:hasDateTimeDescription [ periodo:earliestYear "0250"^^xsd:gYear ;
                    periodo:latestYear "0275"^^xsd:gYear ] ] ;
    foaf:page <https://web.archive.org/web/20200331180155/http://chersonesos.org/?p=history_ant> .

