<http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p0j9r7233z7> a skos:Concept ;
    periodo:spatialCoverageDescription "Poland" ;
    dcelements:language "en" ;
    dcterms:language <http://lexvo.org/id/iso639-1/en> ;
    dcterms:source [ bibo:locator "20" ] ;
    dcterms:spatial <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q36> ;
    skos:altLabel "Brześć-Kujawski Culture"@en,
        "Late Lengyel"@en ;
    skos:editorialNote "The very late end date of the 95% range is very improbable, as at this time numerous other cultures are attested (e. g. funnel beaker). Therefore, in this case, the 68% range of the 14C dates was given precedence. " ;
    skos:inScheme <http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p0j9r72> ;
    skos:note """"The date when Late Lengyel IIIB ended is more uncertain, since we have only one assemblage associ-
ated with a short-life sample. The model suggests that Late Lengyel IIIB ended in 3905–2715 CAL B.C.
(95% probability; end IIIB) (FIG. 9), probably in 3805–3370 CAL B.C. (68% probability). This is rather later than the end of Late Lengyel activity at Racot 18, which occurred in 4035–3990 CAL B.C. (95% prob-
ability; End Racot Late Lengyel) (FIG . 10), probably in 3970–3915 CAL B.C. (68% probability). It is currently not clear, however, whether Racot 18 ended before the demise of Late Lengyel IIIB ceramics elsewhere.
Neither the animal bone from pit B354 at Bodzia 1 (Poz-43555) nor any of the dates on unidentified charcoal from this phase (FIG . 9) need be any later than the 40th century CAL B.C. Late Lengyel IIIB ceramics may
continue later into the 4th millennium but, on present evidence, they need not have done so and, again, only further radiocarbon dates on short-life material associated with diagnostic cultural material will demonstrate
this unequivocally."
""" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Late Lengyel" ;
    time:intervalFinishedBy [ skos:prefLabel "-3805/-3370" ;
            time:hasDateTimeDescription [ periodo:earliestYear "-3805"^^xsd:gYear ;
                    periodo:latestYear "-3370"^^xsd:gYear ] ] ;
    time:intervalStartedBy [ skos:prefLabel "-4400/-4300" ;
            time:hasDateTimeDescription [ periodo:earliestYear "-4400"^^xsd:gYear ;
                    periodo:latestYear "-4300"^^xsd:gYear ] ] .

