<http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p0t3585kxnj> a skos:Concept ;
    periodo:spatialCoverageDescription "Central Texas" ;
    dcelements:language "en" ;
    dcterms:language <http://lexvo.org/id/iso639-1/en> ;
    dcterms:source [ bibo:locator "p. 5, fig. 2; p. 20; p. 39" ] ;
    dcterms:spatial <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q1439> ;
    skos:altLabel "Archaic Era"@en ;
    skos:editorialNote "Temporal coverage takes start from start of first subperiod, end from end of last subperiod; the label and the period-subperiod relationship is drawn from the chart on p. 5." ;
    skos:inScheme <http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p0t3585> ;
    skos:note "\"The Early Archaic period of the Plateau, in some places beginning around 6500 B.C. or earlier, as at the Wilson-Leonard site (41WM235), represents almost three millennia when bison were supposedly absent from the region (cf. Dillehay 1974)\" (p.20); \"I provisionally stop the Late Archaic period around A.D. 600... Nevertheless, one should underscore the fact that some cultural and considerable economic continuity tied the end of the Late Archaic period with what came directly afterwards. In fact, of all the period boundaries set in the present paper, that for the ending of the Late Archaic II subperiod is the most subjective and bothersome... If the informed reader wishes to terminate the Late Archaic period at A.D. 1200, I will not argue. Or if the reader wants to stop the period at around A.D. 400 (or later), when very small \"dart\" points of the Darl and Figueroa sort appear in the region, that is another possibility\" (pp. 39-40)." ;
    skos:prefLabel "Archaic Era" ;
    time:intervalFinishedBy [ skos:prefLabel "A.D. 400/A.D. 1200" ;
            time:hasDateTimeDescription [ periodo:earliestYear "0400"^^xsd:gYear ;
                    periodo:latestYear "1200"^^xsd:gYear ] ] ;
    time:intervalStartedBy [ skos:prefLabel "around 6500 B.C. or earlier" ;
            time:hasDateTimeDescription [ time:year "-6499"^^xsd:gYear ] ] ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p0qkjhbrq6c> .

