<http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p0ndpcq> a skos:ConceptScheme ;
    dcterms:source <http://www.worldcat.org/oclc/780936246> ;
    skos:editorialNote """"Gassner, Verena; Jilek, Sonja; Ladstätter, Sabine (2002–2003): Am Rande des Reiches. Die Römer in Österreich. Österreichische Geschichte 15 v. Chr.–378 n. Chr. Vienna: Ueberreuter. <http://www.worldcat.org/oclc/780936246>" is one of the most important contributions which still represents the most comprehensive account of the Roman period's archaeology for the former Roman provinces on the territory of present-day Austria. This is especially true for the holistic presentation of all aspects of archaeology concerning the province of Noricum. Moreover, this volume presents a comprehensive overview of the various periods of Roman-time Noricum. 
This authority contains yet the most important entries for the Roman province of Noricum (mostly today's Austria and parts of Slovenia, Italy, and Germany). """ .

