<http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p0b6j5m> a skos:ConceptScheme ;
    dcterms:source [ dcterms:creator [ foaf:name "Larissa Sedikova" ],
                [ foaf:name "Adam Rabinowitz" ] ;
            dcterms:issued "2020" ;
            dcterms:title "Chersonesos South Region Periodization" ] ;
    skos:editorialNote "Periodization developed in the course of excavations carried out by the joint Institute of Classical Archaeology (University of Texas)/National Preserve of Tauric Chersonesos project in the South Region of Chersonesos in Crimea from 2001-2006, refined for database implementation and final publication between 2008 and 2020." .

<http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p0dx86h> a skos:ConceptScheme ;
    dcterms:source <http://dx.doi.org/10.23865/noasp.141> ;
    skos:editorialNote """The chronology (given in calibrated years BC/BCE) divides the Southeast Norwegian Stone Age into main phases and sub-phases that are recognized by significant cultural characteristics. Based on recent research, the foundation for the divisions is more solid concerning the Mesolithic, while the Neolithic largely builds on South Scandinavian chronology and to a lesser degree is founded in regional data (Damlien et al. 2021:15).

Steinalderen i Sørøst-Norge. Faglig program for steinalderundersøkelser ved Kulturhistorisk museum [The Stone Age in Southeast Norway. Academic program for Stone Age research at the Museum of Cultural History] (Damlien et al. 2021) contains a summary of updated research and results from more than 400 Stone Age sites excavated between 2000 and 2017. It also defines specific future research challenges and goals. The program is in daily use by researchers, as well as the regional and national government as a basis for the culture heritage management in the region.""" .

<http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p0jgnvq> a skos:ConceptScheme ;
    dcterms:source <http://www.worldcat.org/oclc/1028624877> .

<http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p0m448v> a skos:ConceptScheme ;
    dcterms:source [ dcterms:creator [ foaf:name "Solveig A. Turpin" ] ;
            dcterms:issued "1991" ;
            dcterms:title "The radiocarbon chronology of the Lower Pecos River Region" ] ;
    skos:editorialNote "While the publication uses general period divisions as headers, it is clear that the author favors the period terms proposed by D. Dibble as apparently reported in E. Prewitt's unpublished 1983 MA thesis in the Department of Geography at the University of Texas at Austin (\"Remote Sensing of Archaeological Remains in the Stockton Plateau Region of Texas\"; this seems to be what is indicated by the column \"Dibble in Prewitt 1983 Periods\" in fig. 1.1, p. 11). Therefore, in some cases the Dibble terms have been used as the primary labels for the periods recorded here." .

