<http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p07h9k6> a skos:ConceptScheme ;
    dcterms:source [ dcterms:abstract """The document shows the chrono-cultural categories that are employed to classify archaeological entities within the Sistema de Información Arqueológica (Archaelogical Information System, SIA+) of Incipit CSIC.
Chrono-cultural categories are not exactly periods. They have strong chronological semantics but also possess cultural meaning. This is an arguable way to categorise archaeological entities, but nevertheless they have been used by Incipit CSIC on the SIA+ for over 18 years, and currently characterise over 200.000 entities from Galicia and neighbouring areas in NW Spain.""" ;
            dcterms:creator [ foaf:name "César Gonzalez-Perez" ],
                [ foaf:name "César Parcero Oubiña" ] ;
            dcterms:issued "2014" ;
            dcterms:title "SIA+ Chrono-Cultural Categories" ] .

