    skos:editorialNote """As of June 2020, this authority contains only the complete periodization of the first four major rows of spatial coverage in Priestley's chart ("America", "Africa", "China", and "India"), as they appear at https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/1e/A_New_Chart_of_History_color.jpg. Note that this digital image, derived from a print work in the library of the University of Oregon and used in an interactive project by Daniel Rosenberg at https://pages.uoregon.edu/infographics/timeline/pages/index.html, appears to be from the original 1769 publication, but someone has added the United States after the English colonies at 1776 (after the publication date). We have included this addition, which seems to be specific to this particular chart. 

