<http://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p086kj9> a skos:ConceptScheme ;
    dcterms:source [ dcterms:abstract "The Digital Index of North American Archaeology (DINAA) project is developing the first online, integrated, and comprehensive database of evidence for North America’s human settlement. DINAA provides a free and open framework to examine multidisciplinary questions of human-environmental relationships, at multiple geospatial and temporal scales. The project launched in 2011 as a publicly accessible compilation of existing archaeological site file, collection, and report data from multiple regional, state, and local repositories, linked with environmental and paleoenvironmental datasets. DINAA embraces current best practices in scientific data-management. These include open standards and open licensing, transparent version control (of both data and source code), Linked Data, and iterative development. In consultation and cooperation with government, academic, and tribal stakeholders, our team is now completing the first ‘proof of concept’ phase of the project. We have already linked site file information from much of the eastern United States, demonstrating the capability to develop a truly continental database." ;
            dcterms:creator [ foaf:name "Joshua Wells" ],
                [ foaf:name "Kelsey Noack Myers" ],
                [ foaf:name "Sarah W. Kansa" ],
                [ foaf:name "Sephen Yerka" ],
                [ foaf:name "Eric C. Kansa" ],
                [ foaf:name "R Carl DeMuth" ],
                [ foaf:name "David G. Anderson" ],
                [ foaf:name "Thaddeus Bissett" ] ;
            dcterms:date "2014-10-09"^^xsd:date ;
            dcterms:issued "2012" ;
            dcterms:title "Digital Index of North American Archaeology (DINAA)" ;
            foaf:page <http://ux.opencontext.org/blog/archaeology-site-data/> ] .

